roboparty-rp-head (0.2.1-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Add interface_type ("can" / "canfd") to the C++ API, pybind module,
    Python controller and CLI; default to "can" for this classic-CAN head.
  * Stagger the periodic zero-MIT refresh: one axis every 250 ms with a
    1 ms guard, so each axis is still refreshed every 500 ms. This avoids
    classic CAN TEC spikes and ERROR-PASSIVE after a session.
  * Add the "teleop" CLI subcommand and keyboard teleop (a/d yaw,
    w/s pitch, q quit), with scripted --demo mode.
  * Rename the internal Python modules to rphead_controller, rphead_cli and
    rphead_teleop to avoid generic module names.
  * Require roboparty-motors (>= 2.3.4) for the classic CAN LRO path.

 -- changchuanyong <1984715306@qq.com>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0800

roboparty-rp-head (0.2.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.2.0: pure-Python head controller and CLI built on motors_py.
  * Add offline tests and CI (python-tests + amd64/arm64 deb builds).
  * Install roboparty_head to the install prefix (default /opt/roboparty)/lib/python3/dist-packages and
    expose the roboparty-head launcher.
  * Build against roboparty-motors 2.3 (void set_motor_zero).

